  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "Absolute bioavailability is 37%, and a high-fat meal raises combined exposure 3.1-fold. It is more than 99% bound to plasma protein, and most of a dose leaves unchanged in the feces.",
    "substance": "A hydrochloride salt whose free base weighs 482.62, with a pKa of 7.05.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA as 150 mg hard capsules, taken as 600 mg twice daily.",
    "safety": "No boxed warning and no contraindications. Hepatotoxicity (41%) and constipation (39%) are the most common adverse reactions.",
    "indication": "Adjuvant treatment after tumor resection of biomarker-selected non-small cell lung cancer, and treatment of metastatic biomarker-selected lung cancer.",
    "mechanism": "Inhibits the ALK and RET kinases, blocking ALK phosphorylation and downstream STAT3 and AKT signaling."
  },
  "tell": "An ALK and RET kinase inhibitor with a large food effect: a high-fat meal raises combined exposure 3.1-fold.",
